---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Poetry - Claire Nyquist"
    description="Poetry by Claire Nyquist. Coming soon: Mummies & Wildflowers, a collection of poems about birth, bodies, nature, love, and the end."
    image="/images/gifs/poetry-poster.webp"
>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl name-gradient mb-6">Poetry</h1>
        </div>

        <!-- Book Section -->
        <div
            class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-center lg:items-start justify-center gap-10 lg:gap-16 mb-16"
        >
            <!-- The proof copy, flipping through -->
            <div class="book-video w-full max-w-lg lg:max-w-xl flex-shrink-0">
                <!-- Plain video everywhere; if autoplay is blocked (low
                     power mode), the poster frame stands in. -->
                <video
                    src="/videos/poetry.mp4"
                    poster="/images/gifs/poetry-poster.webp"
                    autoplay
                    muted
                    loop
                    playsinline
                    preload="auto"
                    aria-label="Hands flipping through a printed hardcover proof copy of the poetry book Mummies & Wildflowers on a wooden table."
                    width="1080"
                    height="1270"
                    class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg shadow-lg"
                ></video>
            </div>

            <!-- Coming soon + blurb -->
            <div class="max-w-md lg:pt-8 text-center lg:text-left">
                <p
                    class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600 mb-3"
                >
                    Coming soon
                </p>
                <h2
                    class="font-space-grotesk text-3xl md:text-4xl text-gray-900 mb-2"
                >
                    Mummies &amp; Wildflowers
                </h2>
                <p class="text-gray-500 italic mb-8">poems</p>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    Spanning four years of Minnesota weather, Mummies &amp;
                    Wildflowers moves through a full circle of seasons and
                    comes out the other side in bloom.
                </p>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    These are poems that hold two things at once and refuse to
                    choose: the preserved dead and the flower, the grief and
                    the appetite, the lover and the microscope, the cold breeze
                    and the reason to roll the window down anyway.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Sugar Skulls, the book version, verbatim from the manuscript
             (each line is its own element so the breaks survive, with a
             hanging indent; stanzas are their own blocks so the gaps survive). -->
        <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto pb-4">
            <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600 mb-3">
                From the book
            </p>
            <h2
                class="font-space-grotesk text-2xl md:text-3xl text-gray-900 mb-6"
            >
                Sugar Skulls
            </h2>
            <div class="poem text-gray-700">
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are skulls of sugar</p>
                    <p>We are skulls with marigolds blooming from empty eye sockets</p>
                    <p>We are on reprieve from oblivion</p>
                    <p>Which our beloved ancestors have already encountered</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are hominin bones decorated with saw marks from stone blades</p>
                    <p>Cannibalized and recycled protein (please don’t recoil)</p>
                    <p>Sustaining those who will go on to leave a genetic legacy</p>
                    <p>Up until the most beautiful present</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are bones of calcium carbonate left to bleach in the sun</p>
                    <p>We are bones left on mountaintops for a sky burial to be choked down by the vultures</p>
                    <p>You were born to fly on the sky looking on the world</p>
                    <p>With a scavenger’s ugly-beautiful hooked head</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are bones left in the sediment</p>
                    <p>Encased in soft mud and then fossilized to rock beyond chemical recognition</p>
                    <p>We are bones left for all eternity or at least until</p>
                    <p>The Earth’s crust is returned once more to the underworld of lava</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are drafting on the breeze</p>
                    <p>Of our atmosphere churned through the trillion little green cells, cyanobacteria</p>
                    <p>We are stinking putrid rotting flesh</p>
                    <p>Given new life in an emerald fly’s shimmering iridescent body</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are bones decorated with myosin sliding in the tissue of skeletal muscle</p>
                    <p>Slow-twitch fast-twitch, what have you</p>
                    <p>Bones decorated with the most beautiful and unlikely and complex molecules</p>
                    <p>Huge chains of carbons and an unlikely bath of liquid water</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are bones decorated with a dusting of fertile pollen from perfect blossoms</p>
                    <p>Which god willing archeologists of the future will encounter</p>
                    <p>Speculating that we honored our dead with flowers</p>
                    <p>(Please God, let those future archeologists be around to find us)</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are carrion now and later</p>
                    <p>You are dried flesh now and later</p>
                    <p>We are flesh sacks against all entropic odds</p>
                    <p>You will dry up like Liu Cixin’s human jerky in chaotic eras of too many or too few suns</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>You will be dead</p>
                    <p>You better make the most of the eidetic sparkle while your chemistry continues</p>
                    <p>You better take those saw-decorated long bones and suck out the marrow</p>
                    <p>Like a hungry ancestor shattering open an animal bone for the rich nutrition</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>We are the lucky ones for our brief reprieve from the unconscious darkness</p>
                    <p>You grew in a cell cluster from 3.7 billion years of unlikely legacy</p>
                    <p>There’s nothing before or after but lack of this perfect playful world</p>
                    <p>If I knew how to spend it I would help you</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>So in the teeth of this neanderthal skull</p>
                    <p>In the sun-bleached metacarpals grasping these staggering odds</p>
                    <p>I beg of you</p>
                    <p>Soak up every photon shone from our star which falls on your beautiful face</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <p>I’m just a fragment of fraying DNA,</p>
                    <p>And so are you, beloved</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-6">
                First appeared in the Minnesota Poets Collective Quarterly
                Newsletter, August 2025.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <style>
        .poem p {
            font-style: italic;
            font-size: 1.125rem;
            line-height: 1.8;
            margin: 0;
            padding-left: 1.6em;
            text-indent: -1.6em;
        }
        @media (max-width: 640px) {
            .poem p {
                font-size: 1.0625rem;
                line-height: 1.7;
            }
        }
    </style>

</BaseLayout>
